A||N||18||Eric_PA||84 just put on road after 8 years!||||6||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||11-25-2000||09:04 PM||||Well I just put my Red 84 on the road today. It has been a long journey, but it made it. I bought this car two years ago in pieces, I don't know why, but just wanted to buy it. Lucky for me it still had a title. I must say it was missing the following:<P>No seats<BR>No gas tank<BR>It had an engine block with the wrong pistons<BR>had no trunk deck lid<BR>brake lines where cut up<BR>no rear rotors or calipers<BR>ne ebrake lever<P>Lets just say the car was going to the bone yard and I didn't want it to so I decided to take it off of someones hands. I ended up putting way too much money into it. Don't want to say how much. Lets just say I recently bought a fastback for less than what's in this car. The 84 was originally going to get a HO Quad 4 but decided that it's now going into the Fastback. By the way this 84 has not seen the road since 1992! I definately brought it back from the dead. I have to thank my friend Matt for letting me put the engine in the trunk of his VW Golf when we found it in the boneyard with only 50000 miles on it. I figure the engine was in great shape since the donor car had a FOCOA sticker on it. <P>Well to make this short I put on over 200 miles on it today and right when I got in front of my place it died on me for no reason. I didn't look at it yet, but it seems like it developed a fuel problem. I will find out tomorrow. I hope it's something simple cause I want to get started with the suspension on my GT and get things ready for the winter swap. I will have to find out how to post pics, because this car has come a long ways from when I got it.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 Fastback<BR>Red 84 4 speed<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||11-26-2000||10:09 AM||||<BR>Congrats on the re-birth.  A fine acomplishment, not a thing that many Fiero Freaks are willing to attempt.<P>Resolve that problem, too much time invested to let that problem hold you back.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||11-26-2000||01:22 PM||||Well I found the problem. It's a bad fuel injector. It is just about dumping gas into the throttle body. Another problem is that I forgot to put in the bolts on the roof to seal up the sunroof. There was literaly inches of water on the floor. I pulled the seats out and the carpeting to dry it out for now. I ran out of time today to completely take care of the water problem but will this Tuesday and get it inspected. Can't wait, finally have a winter Fiero.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 Fastback <BR>Red 84 4 speed<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-26-2000||01:58 PM||||Nice job - I admire your patience and tenacity.  Didja take "before" pictures?? I hope so - that'd be impressive, to compare the "before" to the "after"!||||reg||6
Z||000004||Eric_PA||11-26-2000||02:09 PM||||I sure do have pics and a scanner. I have to scan them and figure out how to post them. This car wasn't supposed to be my project car, but the more I dug into it the more I felt I had to replace things. Was my first Fiero and learned a lot from it. Now I'm ready to move on to my newly acquired GT.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 Fastback<BR>Red 84 4 speed<P>||||reg||1
